  "question": "If $a = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) + \\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$ and $b = \\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt{3}) - \\cot^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$, then find the value of $a+b$.",
  "answeroption": "",
  "explanation": "**Step 1:** Evaluate $a$: $a = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) + \\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\left(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\frac{2\\pi}{3} = \\frac{11\\pi}{12}$.\n\n**Step 2:** Evaluate $b$: $b = \\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt{3}) - \\cot^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3} - \\left(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3} - \\frac{2\\pi}{3} = -\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n\n**Step 3:** Calculate $a+b$: $\\frac{11\\pi}{12} + \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{11\\pi}{12} - \\frac{4\\pi}{12} = \\frac{7\\pi}{12}$.",
